WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.660
Aisha is a licensed life producer.

2
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:05.500
Marcus asks whether she can promise that every application will be

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.200
approved. She cannot. A producer's role and authority have limits.

4
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:15.180
In a typical insurer agency relationship, the insurer is the principal

5
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.400
and the producer is its agent.

6
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.920
The principal authorizes the agent to perform specified acts on its

7
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:26.000
behalf. The producer may have duties to applicants and insureds as

8
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.040
well. The word agent identifies a relationship; it does not mean

9
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:34.100
permission to rewrite a policy or ignore underwriting.

10
00:00:34.914 --> 00:00:38.754
Express authority is specifically granted, often in the producer's written

11
00:00:38.754 --> 00:00:42.594
agreement. For example, an insurer may authorize Aisha to solicit

12
00:00:42.594 --> 00:00:46.094
applications and collect an initial premium using its approved receipt.

13
00:00:46.514 --> 00:00:48.674
She should read what the grant permits and what it excludes.

14
00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:52.574
A life producer ordinarily does not have unrestricted power to bind

15
00:00:52.574 --> 00:00:54.694
coverage or waive application requirements.

16
00:00:55.114 --> 00:00:58.414
If Marcus asks for a guarantee outside her authority, the correct

17
00:00:58.414 --> 00:01:01.994
response is to explain the limits and obtain the insurer's decision,

18
00:01:02.374 --> 00:01:03.734
not invent an approval.

19
00:01:04.428 --> 00:01:08.388
Implied authority includes actions reasonably necessary to carry out the

20
00:01:08.388 --> 00:01:13.308
express grant. If Aisha is authorized to solicit and submit applications,

21
00:01:13.908 --> 00:01:17.908
explaining how to complete the approved form may be incidental to

22
00:01:17.908 --> 00:01:21.548
that work. Implied authority is not a way to bypass an

23
00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:26.488
express restriction. Changing a premium rate, deleting an exclusion, or

24
00:01:26.488 --> 00:01:31.600
promising an underwriting result is not justified
merely because it would help make a sale.

26
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:35.308
Always connect the incidental action to the task the principal actually

27
00:01:35.308 --> 00:01:39.722
authorized. Apparent authority concerns what a third party reasonably

28
00:01:39.722 --> 00:01:42.962
believes because of the principal's words or conduct.

29
00:01:43.822 --> 00:01:47.722
Suppose the insurer presents a person to customers as authorized to

30
00:01:47.722 --> 00:01:52.162
perform a particular task, and a customer reasonably relies on that

31
00:01:52.162 --> 00:01:57.262
presentation. That can create an apparent-authority issue even if a private

32
00:01:57.262 --> 00:02:02.302
instruction is narrower. The producer's unsupported statement, I can

33
00:02:02.302 --> 00:02:04.782
do anything, is not enough by itself.

34
00:02:05.662 --> 00:02:10.102
Look for conduct attributable to the principal and reasonable reliance.

35
00:02:11.082 --> 00:02:15.342
Whether an insurer is legally bound depends on the actual facts

36
00:02:15.342 --> 00:02:20.560
and applicable law. A captive or exclusive producer generally represents

37
00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.200
one insurer or affiliated group.

38
00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.140
An independent producer may work with several insurers.

39
00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:32.620
Neither label replaces licensing, appointment or contract requirements.

40
00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:37.340
In Maryland, written appointment documentation and the insurer's producer

41
00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.420
register have their own rules.

42
00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:45.100
A business entity's relationship and an individual's authority should not be

43
00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:50.220
assumed identical. For this lesson, remember that a producer's contract

44
00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:54.660
governs the working relationship, while a state license and an insurer

45
00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:59.460
appointment answer separate regulatory and authorization questions.

46
00:03:00.186 --> 00:03:05.266
Aisha's useful work is accurate fact gathering, honest explanation, careful

47
00:03:05.266 --> 00:03:09.606
handling of premiums and private information, and prompt transmission of the

48
00:03:09.606 --> 00:03:15.026
application. She must not forge a signature, conceal a material answer,

49
00:03:15.666 --> 00:03:18.146
or describe a nonguaranteed value as guaranteed.

50
00:03:19.426 --> 00:03:22.206
If she lacks an answer, she should verify it.

51
00:03:23.106 --> 00:03:26.606
When you classify authority on an exam, ask where it came

52
00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:32.166
from: a direct grant, a necessary incidental action, or the principal's

53
00:03:32.166 --> 00:03:33.406
appearance to the customer.

54
00:03:34.306 --> 00:03:37.206
Then choose the action that remains within that authority.
